1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,895
Three thermostat numbers that are worth real money.

2
00:00:03,015 --> 00:00:04,538
Number one: eight hours.

3
00:00:04,658 --> 00:00:13,263
The Department of Energy says setting your thermostat back for at least eight hours a day can save as much as ten percent a year on heating and cooling.

4
00:00:13,383 --> 00:00:14,915
Number two: nine hundred.

5
00:00:15,035 --> 00:00:20,985
ENERGY STAR says the average household spends more than nine hundred dollars a year on heating and cooling.

6
00:00:21,105 --> 00:00:23,654
Ten percent of that is about ninety dollars.

7
00:00:23,774 --> 00:00:25,277
Number three: three in ten.

8
00:00:25,397 --> 00:00:32,896
Only about three in ten homes with a programmable or smart thermostat actually let it adjust the temperature automatically.

9
00:00:33,016 --> 00:00:37,515
Put them together: the savings are there, and most people just aren't using them.

10
00:00:37,635 --> 00:00:39,583
So tonight, set it back while you sleep.

11
00:00:39,703 --> 00:00:42,088
Three thermostat numbers worth real money.
